# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization.
#
# `text=auto` alone only guarantees LF in the STORED blob. Checkout still honours
# each machine's core.autocrlf, which the Windows Git installer sets to `true`,
# so a fresh clone lands CRLF on disk and VS Code warns:
#
#   "This file uses 'LF' line endings, but Git is configured to convert them to
#    'CRLF' the next time the file is checked out."
#
# That warning is harmless -- Git normalizes back to LF on commit either way, so
# it never produces diff noise. `eol=lf` pins the WORKING TREE to LF too, which
# makes the result identical on every machine and silences it for everyone.
#
# Safe here specifically: the entire tree is already LF, and there are no
# .bat/.cmd/.ps1/.sh files that would want CRLF. Add an exception line if one is
# ever introduced.
* text=auto eol=lf
